\title{RedKinNet: Selection of Unrelated Individuals from Kinship Networks}
\description{
Selects sets of mutually unrelated individuals from pairwise kinship estimates. Relatedness above a user-defined threshold is represented as an undirected graph, and each connected component (family network) is resolved as a maximum independent set problem, combining structural rules and graph reductions with exact resolution of the remaining ambiguity. Ambiguous choices can be resolved at random or according to covariate-based criteria, and node-level diagnostics document the reason for every retained or discarded individual.
